{
  "manufacturer": "Armstrong Fluid Technology",
  "manufacturer_slug": "armstrong-fluid-technology",
  "model": "SE-A10 chiller plant controller",
  "model_slug": "se-a10",
  "aliases": [
    "SE-A10",
    "SE-A 10",
    "Armstrong SE-A10",
    "90.7671"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Chiller plant controller (chillers and chilled water pumps)",
  "applies_to": "Armstrong SE-A10 chilled water plant controls with no condenser water side; the object list covers up to 3 chillers and 3 chilled water pumps.",
  "summary": "The SE-A10 controls a small chilled water plant with up to 3 chillers and 3 chilled water pumps and no condenser water or tower points. Its BACnet object list gives plant start/stop, alarm reset, plant load, power and efficiency, chilled water temperatures and flow, chiller and pump status, alarms, drive data and Hand/Auto overrides.",
  "bacnet_transport": [],
  "firmware": "BACnet communication interface Rev 24.111",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The data-points sheet titles the table BACnet but does not say whether it is BACnet IP or MS/TP.",
    "Mode objects (AV) use 0 = Not Used, 1 = Hand, 2 = Off, 3 = Auto. Duty/standby, chiller duty and chiller state objects are coded values; the codes are in each point's states.",
    "Hand/Auto BVs and Hand Command BVs, plus the Hand Speed / Hand Position AOs, let the BMS run a valve or pump by hand. Set Lead objects act only when the written value changes.",
    "Units for temperatures, pressures and flows follow the controller's unit setting (the PDF lists the options).",
    "The PDF table is on pages 7-9. One Reserved AI is left out."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "The SE-A10 publishes a fixed BACnet object list. Start and stop the plant with BO 1 Remote Start, write the zone setpoint (AV 2), and read BI 1 Plant Status, plant load, chilled water temperatures, plant power and efficiency. Use BO 3 to reset alarms. Per-chiller, per-pump and per-valve alarms, run feedbacks and Hand/Auto overrides are there if the BMS needs more detail.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 1",
        "name": "Remote Start",
        "why": "Plant start/stop from the BMS (1 = start)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "Zone 1 Setpoint",
        "why": "Zone 1 control setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 3",
        "name": "Alarm Reset",
        "why": "Reset plant alarms (positive edge)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1",
        "name": "Plant Status",
        "why": "Plant on/off status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "Plant Load",
        "why": "Plant cooling load, tons"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1001",
        "name": "chws Temp",
        "why": "Chilled water supply temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1002",
        "name": "chwr Temp",
        "why": "Chilled water return temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "Total Plant Power Consumption",
        "why": "Total plant power, kW"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Plant Efficiency",
        "why": "Plant efficiency, kW/ton"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 10",
        "name": "Refrigerant Leak Alarm",
        "why": "Refrigerant leak detected"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BO 1 Remote Start (0 = Stop, 1 = Start) starts and stops the plant from the BMS. The data-points sheet says nothing more about local/remote selection.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The data-points sheet does not give the device instance, MAC address, baud rate or IP settings; get them from the controller setup."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "BO 3 Alarm Reset acts on a positive edge (0 to 1); write 0 again before the next reset.",
      "Hand/Auto BVs and Hand Command / Hand Speed objects override the plant sequence; leave them in Auto for normal operation.",
      "Mode AVs are coded 0-3 (1 = Hand, 2 = Off, 3 = Auto); writing them takes that equipment out of automatic sequencing.",
      "Set Lead Chiller / Pump objects act only when the value changes, so rewriting the same value does nothing."
    ]
  },
